Answer: (A) {2,4,5}
Why and working: A={2,4,6} and B={5,6}. Their union includes six, but six triggers both, so remove it to leave the three exclusive outcomes.
Why not the others: (B) includes an outcome triggering both. (C) gives the intersection rather than exactly one. (D) neither event occurs for these draws.

Answer: (A) ℝ×{4}×{−2}
Why and working: Each point is (4,t,−2). Swapping the first two coordinates gives (t,4,−2), with t still arbitrary.
Why not the others: (B) moves the variable to the third coordinate. (C) also swaps the fixed third coordinate incorrectly. (D) gives the original set.
